IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, DATE HELPERS. These are counting conventions, not provisions of the
-- Regulations: the text says "three months starting on the date", "28 days starting
-- with the date", "the year following", and never says how to count them.
-- Each convention taken here is registered in NOTES.md (fork register F1 to F4).

§ `Date helpers`

-- The stable prelude has no YMD (NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept").
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD y m d MEANS Date d m y

-- F1. "N days starting with D" is read inclusively: D is the first day of the
-- period, so the last day is D plus N minus 1.
-- Example: 28 days starting with 1 March end on 28 March.
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of days starting with` first n MEANS first PLUS (n MINUS 1)

-- F2. "N months starting on D" ends the day before the corresponding date N months
-- later (D = 15 January, 3 months: ends 14 April). Where the target month has no
-- corresponding date (D = 31 January, 1 month), the period is taken to end on the
-- last day of the target month. The Regulations do not say; see NOTES.md.
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of months starting on` first n MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY target EQUALS DATE_DAY first
    THEN target MINUS 1
    ELSE target
    WHERE
        target MEANS `add months` first n

-- F3. A tax year starts on 6 April and ends on 5 April; it is named by the calendar
-- year in which it starts (regulation 24(1) says only "year means a tax year").
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax year in which the day falls` day MEANS
    IF day AT LEAST YMD (DATE_YEAR day) 4 6
    THEN DATE_YEAR day
    ELSE DATE_YEAR day MINUS 1

GIVEN taxYear IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the tax year` taxYear MEANS YMD taxYear 4 6

GIVEN taxYear IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the tax year` taxYear MEANS YMD (taxYear PLUS 1) 4 5

-- F4. Whole days between two dates, counted from the serial numbers of the dates.
-- (days between is in actus-daycount, not in daydate, on the stable binary.)
GIVEN earlier IS A DATE
      later IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` earlier `to` later MEANS DATE_SERIAL later MINUS DATE_SERIAL earlier

-- The earlier of two dates (used where a regulation gives alternative time limits and
-- the earliest is taken; NOTES.md, fork F18).
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` a `and` b MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b
